.TH JSONDIFF 1
.SH NAME
jsondiff \\- compare desired and observed JSON documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jsondiff
jsondiff --desired FILE --observed FILE [--format json|ndjson] [--ignore POINTER]
.br
[--set-path POINTER] [--numeric-tolerance NUMBER]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Produces typed, machine-readable JSON differences. Ignore and set paths use JSON Pointer notation.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBjsondiff --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
